# Tech Specs Agent — Implementation Walkthrough

## What Was Built

A new **`tech-specs-agent`** that generates structured Technical Specifications from parsed requirements + user stories. It plugs into the existing MCP Host → Java Backend pipeline with zero infrastructure changes.

## Files Created (Python Agent)

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| [server.py](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/server.py) | Entry point: reads stdin JSON, invokes LangGraph, outputs Markdown + JSON |
| [graph.py](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/graph.py) | LangGraph state machine: `generate → validate → retry` (max 3 attempts) |
| [llm.py](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/llm.py) | HuggingFace `Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct` wrapper (4096 max tokens) |
| [schemas/tech_spec.py](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/schemas/tech_spec.py) | Pydantic models: [TechSpecArtifact](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/schemas/tech_spec.py#78-95), [SystemOverview](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/schemas/tech_spec.py#65-70), [DataModel](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/schemas/tech_spec.py#17-25), [APIDesign](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/schemas/tech_spec.py#35-37), etc. |
| [utils.py](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/utils.py) | File I/O helpers |
| [requirements.txt](file:///c:/Users/Vishal.bhardwaj/SDLC/Agentic_Sys/Agentic_Sys/agents/tech_specs_agent/requirements.txt) | `langgraph`, `pydantic`, `huggingface-hub`, `python-dotenv` |

